{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations and their tests**\n- **Snapshot built from `Domain::node_content` contents and their `NodeContents::fingerprint`.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts that `read_snapshot(&1).fingerprint` equals `fp(\"before\")`.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` checks both `snapshot.content.format()` and `snapshot.fingerprint` against the original. It covers an empty string and a large multi-byte Unicode string.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint`. It also asserts that the content and fingerprint stay \"before\" after the domain changes to \"after\".\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks that the fingerprint of the domain's content matches the retained content's fingerprint.\n- **\"Without another read\".**\n  - `fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` asserts the read log is `[1, 1]` for one `read_snapshot` plus one `read`.\n  - `fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts `[1, 1, 1, 2]` across its mixed reads.\n  - `fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts `[1]` for a single `read_snapshot`, even after the fingerprint is recomputed from the retained content.\n  - Together these show that building the snapshot costs exactly one `node_content` call.\n- **Agent read path.** The agent-side tests, `fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` and `fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]`, assert the recorded `Dependency::Node(_, fingerprint)` values. They also assert the read counts for those paths.\n- **Public shape: `Snapshot::new(content, fingerprint)` and public `content` and `fingerprint` fields.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` builds a snapshot through `new` and asserts both fields. The test crate is external, so it can only use `new`, which matches `#[non_exhaustive]`. `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the export is present.\n- **`Clone` and `Debug` impls.** The struct in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]` uses `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]`, so these impls have no conditional or transformation of their own. Under the testing criteria, an untested obligation is exempt when the code carrying it out has no logic of its own. The text also does not say that Clone or Debug output must stay unchanged. I treat these as exempt.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The `{fixme}` acknowledgments are empty, and none are needed.",
